// Turns bamboo into meals. The room that finally gives biomass
// somewhere to go.
//
// Before this, a tower had nothing to *do* with what it harvested: the
// shelves filled, the mill's outbox backed up, the arms stalled, and a
// shade-seeking route and a sun-seeking one came out at exactly the same
// harvest over a whole region (`SYSTEMS.md` §3.10). Meals are a demand
// that scales with the crew rather than with shelf space, cannot be
// satisfied by stockpiling, and run all day.
#![enable(implicit_some)]
RoomDef(
    id: "room.canteen",
    name: "Canteen",
    short: "CTN",
    // **Opens once the burner is lit**, which is where the opening
    // ends. `SYSTEMS.md` §6.11: a first-turn menu with twenty cards on
    // it is the loudest thing in the game and says nothing, so the menu
    // grows as the tower does. This is a fact about the tower, not the
    // player — the journal (§5.7) is the other kind of unlock and can
    // only filter a menu.
    unlocked_by: "room.burner",
    category: Production,
    width: 2,
    // A thornwright's price: dearer than a mill (4), well short of a
    // salvage rig (8). An early, obvious build rather than a commitment.
    build_cost: [CostEntryDef(item: "item.poles", amount: 5)],
    // Deliberately **not** powered, and it is the only production room
    // that is not. A kitchen that goes dark in a brown-out and stops
    // feeding people turns one bad night into a spiral inside a spiral —
    // and "powered production is a charge sink" is already taught by the
    // thornwright, a room the player chose to build for a reason other
    // than survival.
    recipe: RecipeDef(
        // Ten seconds a batch, which is visible as cooking. Flat out the
        // room makes more than ten times what a full crew eats, so it is
        // buffer-limited and mostly idle — correct for a kitchen, and it
        // means the canteen's *rate* is not what sets bamboo demand.
        // The crew are.
        craft_ticks: 300,
        // **Two bamboo a meal, which is six a day a crew member.**
        //
        // This was authored 2 → 3, a third of a stalk a meal, and that
        // was a straight misreading of the design: `SYSTEMS.md` §4.3
        // states the target twice as "2 bamboo a meal … 6 bamboo a day
        // a crew member … about a fifth of what a fed mill draws", and
        // the ratio it calls "the whole judgement" is that fifth. At
        // 2 → 3 a crew member ate two stalks a day rather than six, the
        // canteen drew about 5% of a mill instead of 20%, and a tower
        // stayed demand-limited on bamboo — which meant the terrain
        // yields still could not be felt, measured at 353 stalks against
        // 351 on two routes eight percent apart in weighted yield. The
        // batch of three and the ten-second craft are both kept; only
        // the price is corrected.
        inputs: [IoEntryDef(item: "item.bamboo", amount: 6, buffer_max: 12)],
        outputs: [IoEntryDef(item: "item.meals", amount: 3, buffer_max: 9)],
    ),
)
